From mdowle at mdowle.plus.com  Sun Jan 20 17:13:53 2013
From: mdowle at mdowle.plus.com (Matthew Dowle)
Date: Sun, 20 Jan 2013 16:13:53 +0000
Subject: [datatable-help] possible bug when running setkey on POSIXct
 column
In-Reply-To: <CAKzGw12kans364JSVb7q7=tbHDKQicLD98xb9ndKwRf8z0Xx6g@mail.gmail.com>
References: <CAGyMscqO6=ri-cwcX6MSuLTpzd0BTGkxTw54F+P8Mevbw_Vj0A@mail.gmail.com>
 <CAAxdm-4uO0qgxyW2xA5WVMwE9qcsSnUho7KEPebTTfecj7qTtQ@mail.gmail.com>
 <CAKzGw12kans364JSVb7q7=tbHDKQicLD98xb9ndKwRf8z0Xx6g@mail.gmail.com>
Message-ID: <0338f5fe3e4fbd7f27e39b1696918f18@imap.plus.net>


Indeed. I reproduced. Now fixed. Well done and thanks statquant.

o setkey could sort 'double' columns (such as POSIXct) incorrectly when 
not the
   last column of the key, #2484. In data.table's C code :
      x[a]>x[b]-tol
   should have been :
      x[a]-x[b]>-tol  [or  x[b]-x[a]<tol ]
   The difference may have been machine/compiler dependent. Many thanks 
to statquant
   for the short reproducible example. Test added.


